# Original description (presenter-editable, idempotency anchor)
la desproporción entre lo mucho que un modelo absorbe y lo poco que alcanza para darle forma a su conducta

# Enriched generation prompt (what image generation consumes)
Create an editorial vector-style symbolic illustration for a tall presentation aside (portrait, about 2:3). Emotional role: a calm, reflective close to a lecture on how LLMs are trained, with quiet wonder at a disproportion rather than alarm. Conceptual metaphor: an immense, dense mass of absorbed material (thousands of tiny near-identical dark marks, fine hatched lines or granular dots pooling into one heavy form in the lower part of the frame, the trillions of tokens of pre-training) is steered by a single slender coral-red contour line: a small, precise stroke that wraps, bends or channels the edge of that mass and gives it a direction and a shape (the thin post-training signal that fixes behavior). The contrast in scale between the vast grounded mass and the lone thin accent line is the whole idea; keep it abstract and non-literal. Visual language: bold flat poster-like editorial vector illustration, thin contour or hand-drawn linework, flat fills, high contrast, symbolic idea-flow composition. Palette and contrast: predominantly white / near-white flat ground with strong negative space in the upper part of the frame; the mass in neutral dark #3B3535 (navy-black grounding shapes allowed); exactly one accent color, red #DA1B2E, used only for the single guiding line; no other colors, no gradients, no 3D, no drop shadows. Exclusions: no photorealism or realistic rendering; no literal scenes (no people, brains, robots, computers, servers, books, libraries, classrooms, offices, landscapes, horizons, buildings); no generic decorative geometry unrelated to the idea; no UI, screenshots, dashboards or charts; no readable text, letters, numbers, code, logos, watermarks or signatures.
